on? Hmm.\nThe standard SMB format: \nbyte0: X (7 bits?) and Y\nActually the format: \"Enemy data: each enemy is 3 bytes: 1st byte = X position (0-15, in 16-pixel units?) and Y; 2nd byte = direction/type...\" Hmm.\n\nLet me not decode. Instead, empirically find the Koopa: teleport step by step and list_sprites.\n\nBut there's a smarter way: the enemy list positions. Byte0 = x-page nibbles? Record1 byte0=0x30 → page 3? Hmm 0x30 = 48. If byte0 is x in 16-px units? Hmm.\n\nActually SMB enemy byte1 (first byte) format: bits 7-4 = X page (high 4 bits of level x / 256?), bits 3-0 = Y (in 16-px units). Second byte: bits 7-6 = direction/flags, bits 5-0 = X within page (in ...). Hmm not sure.\n\nRecord1: 30 C2 00. If byte0=0x30: page=3, y=0? That would be level x ~768-1024. And byte1=0xC2: 0xC2 = 1100 0010. Hmm.\n\nActually I recall the SMB enemy data format precisely:\n- byte 1: X position, bits 7-4 = page (x/256), bits 3-0 = y (in 16-pixel units, y = value*16)\n- byte 2: X position within page (bits 7-6 = something), bits 5-0 = x within page / 4? Hmm.\nActually the well-known format:\n  byte1: bits 4-7 = x page, bits 0-3 = y in blocks\n  byte2: bit 7 = direction? bit 6 = ...? bits 5-0 = x position low? \n  byte3 = enemy type.\n\nLet me look at our list and see which records are at large x (the Koopa is \"far to the right\"). Records:\n1: xpage 3\n2: 0x6B → xpage 6\n3: 0x86 → xpage 8\n4: 0x0F 05 (page entry, sets x page? byte0 low nibble F means \"page entry\": byte1 = new x page? Actually it's a \"page change\" marker: next enemies are on page X.)\n5: 03 06 35\n6: 06 4B B7\n7: BB 00 5B\n8: B7 FB 37\n9: 3B B7 0F\n10: 0B 1B 37\n\nHmm, with page entries resetting. So x pages: rec1 page 3, rec2 page 6, rec3 page 8, then page entry (0x0F, 0x05 → page 5?). Hmm.\n\nThis is getting messy. Let me just scan with the emulator.\n\nPlan: teleport camera in steps of ~500 px, screenshot/list_sprites, and look for a green Koopa. The Koopa is on the ground walking. Its sprite tiles are different from Goomba: Green Koopa uses tiles $30-$35 or similar, palette 7 (or 6?). Actually Koopa uses sprite palette 7 too? Koopa colors: green shell, green body. In SMB, Koopa Troopa uses palette 7? Let me just look.\n\nLet me jump to around x=1500 and scan.\n\nActually, wait. Let me think about where the Koopa Troopa is in 1-1. From memory of SMB 1-1:\n- Goombas at x~22, x~80 (near start, before pipes)\n- The first pipe at x~460\n- Goombas after first pipe\n- Koopa Troopa appears around x~880? Walking.\n- Then second pipe, etc.\n\nActually I recall there's exactly one Koopa Troopa in 1-1, located after the second set of pipes, around the middle, walking toward you. And also a Koopa near the staircase? Hmm.\n\nI'll scan. Let me jump camera to x=1000 (page 3, low 232) and Mario same, step, screenshot.\n\nActually careful: teleporting camera far may cause the streaming to load wrong. Let's do incremental steps of ~500.\n\nLet me write camera=1000, Mario=1000. $071A=3, $071C=232, $006D=3, $0086=232. Step 6, screenshot.\n\nWait, but if Mario's screen x is 0 he's at the left edge; the level streaming might not have loaded the right side. Let me put Mario at camera+100: abs 1100 (page 4 low 76), camera 1000. So $006D=4, $0086=76.\n\nLet me do it."}
