{"type":"thinking","text":"This WorldFoundry doc gives a different (3D-conversion) coordinate system, not the NES level. But the enemy list says:\n\"Green Koopa Troopa × 1: col ~113 (between pyramids / starman area)\"\n\nIn NES tile columns: col 113 → x = 113*16 = 1808 pixels. Hmm! And our enemy record r2 x=1712 (data) — close-ish. And the two \"Goombas\" I saw at abs ~1799/1823... one of them might actually be the Koopa!\n\nBut list_sprites showed BOTH as tiles $FC,$FC,$70-$73 palette 7 — Goomba. Hmm.\n\nHmm, but wait: the WorldFoundry doc's \"col 113\" is in its own 16px tile columns: 113*16 = 1808. Our Goombas at 1799/1823. So the enemy at col ~113 should be a Koopa at x~1808.\n\nHmm, but I saw two Goombas there. Unless the Koopa spawned before/after.\n\nHmm, actually the two enemies at 1799 and 1823 might be Goomba and Koopa... but both had $70-$73 tiles.\n\nWait, let me re-examine that list_sprites output at abs 1897:\nTwo groups: indices 34-39 (x141-173) and 40-45 (x165-...)? Actually:\n- group 1: $FC x141, $FC x149, $70 x141, $71 x149, $72 x141, $73 x149 (y185-201)\n- group 2: $FC x165, $FC x173, $70 x165, $71 x173, $72 x165, $73 x173\nBoth Gooma tiles. Hmm.\n\nBut maybe the Koopa was also there but off my list? The list showed 21 entries: index0 HUD, 1-8 Mario, 34-39 goomba1, 40-45 goomba2. So no Koopa at that moment.\n\nHmm. But maybe the Koopa spawned later at x1808 and walked; by the time I looked (Mario at 1897, camera 1658), the Koopa would be at screen ~150 too... \n\nHmm. So the Koopa should have been visible.\n\nHmm, unless the Koopa despawned/was killed earlier. Actually! When I was bunny-hopping early on, Mario got hit by a Goomba and shrank, then fell in a pit at abs ~1116. That was in a DIFFERENT session (before I reloaded state 1). The state 1 was saved before all that. So in the current timeline (from state 1 via swimming), the Koopa should still be alive.\n\nHmm, but in the swim from state 1, the camera passed x1808. The type watch showed 6 for slots 0,1,2. If the Koopa were there, we'd see a different type.\n\nUnless the Koopa is at a slightly different x and its type... Hmm.\n\nHmm, wait: maybe the Koopa's runtime type IS 6, and the Goomba's is 0? I.e., maybe I have it backwards! Let me check: initially (before I wrote anything), $0016=6 for the enemy that list_sprites showed as tiles $70-$73. But maybe tiles $70-$73 are the KOOPA, not the Goomba!\n\nLet me re-examine: the mapping says Goomba = tiles $70-$73, palette 7. But that mapping might be wrong (it was \"auto-discovered\"). Let me check the actual rendered sprite. Let me read_tile $70 and see the shape. A Goomba is a mushroom-like blob with feet. A Koopa is a turtle with a shell.\n\nLet me look at the screenshot where the type-6 enemy was rendered: at abs 535 it appeared as a small brown blob — consistent with a Goomba. But at this small scale, could also be a Koopa? A Koopa is taller (16x24 vs Goomba 16x16).\n\nHmm, the type-6 enemy was 6 OAM entries: 2 blank $FC + $70,$71,$72,$73 → 16x24 form (2x3 with top blank row). Wait, the Goomba mapping says Goomba is 16x24 with top blank row. But a Koopa is also 16x24! Hmm.\n\nAnd a Goomba is actually 16x16 (2x2). Hmm, in SMB the Goomba metasprite is 2x2 tiles = 16x16, but the sprite form might reserve a 16x24 area.\n\nHmm! So maybe tiles $70-$73 with a blank top row IS the Koopa Troopa, not the Goomba! Let me look at the tile shapes.\n\nLet me read_tile 0x70, 0x71, 0x72, 0x73. If $70 is a dome (Goomba head) → Goomba. If it's a shell/turtle → Koopa.\n\nAlso, the palette 7 = [0F,0F,36,17] = black, black, peach, brown. Peach/brown — a Goomba is brown. A green Koopa would need green. So if the enemy is peach/brown, it's a Goomba. Unless the Koopa in this ROM is... hmm.\n\nBut hold on: the WorldFoundry doc says the Koopa is at col 113 (x~1808), and our two enemies at 1799/1823 were at the right place. Maybe one of them IS the Koopa and it looked brown due to... no.\n\nHmm, I need to just look at the actual sprite more carefully. Let me read the tiles.\n\nActually, let me revisit the screenshot at abs 1897 (with the two enemies). I described \"two Goombas\". The screenshot showed two small brown creatures. A green Koopa would be green. They were brown. So Goombas.\n\nOK so where's the Koopa? The doc says col 113 → x1808, \"between pyramids / starman area\". The pyramids are at cols 134,148 (x2144, 2368). Starman at col 99 (x1584). So \"between pyramids/starman\" ≈ col 113 → x1808. That matches our two enemies at 1799/1823... \n\nHmm, so by the doc, one of those two should be the Koopa. But both looked like Goombas. Unless the doc's count is off.\n\nHmm, hold on! Maybe the Koopa walked away/despawned by the time I looked, and the two Goombas I saw are the \"Goomba ×2 near pyramid A\" at col 130 (x2080)? No, camera 1658 at that time, so x2080 would be at screen 422, off-screen. So the two at 1799/1823 are the \"green koopa area\" ones...\n\nHmm.\n\nOK, let me just directly look at the Koopa. The definitive way: find a moment when it exists. Let me search the live enemy slots over the region x1700-1900 by walking slowly there and doing list_sprites frequently.\n\nActually, the enemy list parse: r2 at x1712 type 8B, r3 at x2144 type B7, r9 at x944 type 0F. The doc says Koopa at x~1808.\n\nHmm, our r2 x=1712 could be the Koopa (type 8B) if my x decoding is off by ~96.\n\nLet me test the hypothesis: data type 0x8B = Green Koopa Troopa. Then r2 spawns a Koopa at x~1712.\n\nBut my type watch showed $0016=6 at slots 0,1 around x1800. Hmm. Unless the Koopa is in a different slot (3,4,5) and I didn't watch it at that moment.\n\nIn the run from abs 806→1000 I watched slots 0,1,2 (22,23,24) and 25,26 in others. Hmm, in the run at abs 1952→~2500 I watched 22,23,24,25,26 (slots 0-4). All 6.\n\nHmm. But that run started at abs 1952, past 1712. So the Koopa (if at 1712) would have spawned in an earlier run. The run from abs ~1353→1547 watched 22,23,24,25,26 → all 6. Hmm, that run was 1353-1547, not reaching 1712.\n\nThe run 1547→1952 (the one where I watched 134,22,23,24,25,26): types were 6 then 0 then 6,6... Let me look at it: \"values\":[0,...,0,6,6,...] for address 22; address 23: 6 then 0; address 24: 6 then 0; address 25: 0; address 26: 0/6. All 6! Hmm. Wait, that was the run \"end_frame 166023\" — let me re-read: watch [134,22,23,24,25,26]:\n- 22: 0..0 then 6 from sample 31\n- 23: 6 at start then 0\n- 24: 0 then 6\n- 25: 6 then 0\n- 26: 6 then 0\nAll 6.\n\nSo at abs 1547-1952, all enemies spawned were type 6. So no Koopa there.\n\nHmm!! Unless the Koopa spawned and despawned between samples (every 5 frames). At 1.3px/frame, an enemy stays on screen for ~100+ frames. So it'd be sampled ~20 times.\n\nI'm confused, but let me just do the decisive test: force the enemy at x1712 by walking there and doing list_sprites right when it spawns.\n\nHmm, actually, let me just re-examine the 1-1 enemy list with the CORRECT x decoding and identify the Koopa record, then go to its x and look.\n\nActually, the WorldFoundry doc's enemy placement for 1-1: Goomba near col 22 (x352), then between pipes etc., Koopa at col ~113 (x1808). Our observation at x~1800: two enemies that looked like Goombas.\n\nWait — maybe one of those WAS the Koopa but I misjudged the color from the small preview! Let me zoom: I can't zoom, but I can sample pixels of the enemy. Or list_sprites gives the palette: both groups had palette 7. A green Koopa would have a green palette (5 or 6?), not 7. Both were 7. So both Goombas.\n\nHmm, but maybe the Koopa in 1-1 uses palette 7 and IS green? Palette 7 = [0F,0F,36,17] = black, black, peach, brown. No green. So no.\n\nHmm, so the Koopa isn't at x1800 either.\n\nOK, you know what — let me just carefully walk 1-1 and list_sprites at each screen, looking for the Koopa. I'll do it with the swim from state 1, at a moderate pace, checking list_sprites at abs intervals. But list_sprites only shows on-screen enemies. As I swim, enemies appear/disappear.\n\nAlternatively: kill all Goombas? no.\n\nHmm, let me think about the enemy record types again, now with the doc:\nData types: r1=00 (Goomba), r2=8B, r3=B7, r5=35, r6=B7, r7=5B, r8=37, r9=0F, r10=37.\nThe doc says 1-1 has 16 Goombas and 1 Koopa. 9 records can't give 17 enemies... unless each reco","truncated":true}
